  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The two Employer and Business Membership Organizations (EBMOs) in North Macedonia play an important role in advancing the collective voice of business and informing policy and law making. Despite making notable progress in modernizing their organizations, they face increasing challenges amid ongoing regional and global crises. These are compounded by the complexity of the EU accession process, which requires expertise the EBMOs currently lack. To remain effective and relevant, they must continue to adapt and embrace innovation, enhance their capacity for evidence-based advocacy, and offer services aligned with evolving member needs.
The ILO&#x2019;s interventions in 2024&#x2013;2025 build on prior activities with the Organisation of Employers of Macedonia (OEM). Following North Macedonia&#x2019;s ratification of ILO Convention 190 in 2023, the ILO supported the OEM in adapting the ACT/EMP Guide on Violence and Harassment to the national context, to serve as the basis for a new training service for its members. Complementary tools have been developed to help enterprises implement workplace policies, as part of broader ILO support in the country. Current efforts focus on scaling up the training and developing scenarios to ensure the long-term sustainability of this new service.
Furthermore, the ILO will support both the OEM and the Business Confederation of Macedonia in articulating the private sector perspective on key challenges to achieving a just transition in North Macedonia. Particular focus is placed on assessing the Nationally Determined Contributions to evaluate their alignment with business needs in the shift to sustainable, low-carbon operations. The EBMOs will also receive support in developing the business case for a just transition and raising awareness of its benefits and opportunities. With additional funding, the ILO will assist the OEM in conducting research to develop evidence-based recommendations aimed at improving productivity and private sector competitivenes.</narrative>
  </description>
